  "label": {
    "bytes": 4411,
    "description": "The Circular Polarization Ratio product, defined as the ratio of the same sense to the opposite sense circularly polarized (CPR = SC / OS) radar returns. These Level 3 products are Derived Data Records (DDRs) generated from multiple Level 1 RDRs. They are mosaics that are produced by ingesting the Level 1 raw RDRs into the ISIS software and orthorectifying them using a combination of spacecraft spice data and spatially tying the data to the LOLA base map. The mosaics are produced for each lunar pole (i.e., regions above +/- 70 deg. latitude). Unlike the lower-level products (Level 1 RDRs and Level 2 CDRs), these products are composed of data sets collected during multiple acquisitions and are produced manually using the ISIS software provided by the Astrogeology branch of the USGS. This is a combined East and West-looking mosaic.",
